# The toolchain the kernel is built with (tools/fetch-wolf,
# tools/fetch-lupin; tools/lib.sh's load_wolf_pin takes one of two
# shapes).
#
# px02: a SOURCE pin. The frame allocator touches memory through the
# HHDM with kw06's `N as *T`, `*p` and `with_addr` (wolf-lang 50830027)
# and kw07's `read_volatile`/`write_volatile` (eb955c3b); both are on
# wolf-lang trunk and in no release yet (0.2.22 is 8e36bc1a). So wolf is
# built from source at this commit, as kw05 pinned af397195:
# tools/fetch-wolf fetches exactly this commit, refuses any other HEAD,
# builds `wolf_driver --locked` stamped with the commit, and checks
# `--version`'s pin clause.
#
# Back to a RELEASE pin when 0.2.23 ships: delete WOLF_LANG_COMMIT and
# set the four lines px01 used (WOLF_VERSION, WOLF_URL, WOLF_SHA256 of
# the x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu archive, WOLF_PIN_COMMIT); tools/fetch-wolf
# then stages the archive by digest and never builds.
WOLF_LANG_COMMIT=eb955c3bbaf534669b048a031f9c0a44dd84f509
# lupin, M-KW step 6's second machine, from its release BY DIGEST.
# Held at 0.1.44 (0.2.22 pairs with 0.1.45): wolf-interp#182, the
# `--target` refusal step 6 records, is open on both.
LUPIN_VERSION=0.1.44
LUPIN_SHA256=e44aae0651693364fe9dc8943fed9b44eb4e9f17ac9362aef4b570ed85387dc0
